# TypeScript Rules

Read `docs/14_CODING_STANDARDS.md` and `docs/09_API_STRATEGY.md`.

## Strict Mode

- `strict: true` always
- **No `any`** — use `unknown` and narrow
- No `@ts-ignore` — use `@ts-expect-error` with explanation if unavoidable
- No non-null assertions (`!`) unless immediately preceded by null check

## Types

- DB types from `src/types/database.ts` (Supabase generated)
- Infer form/action types from Zod: `z.infer<typeof schema>`
- Shared action result: `ActionResult<T>` from `src/types/actions.ts`
- Prefer `interface` for objects; `type` for unions

## Zod

- All schemas in `src/lib/validations/{domain}.ts`
- Share schemas between React Hook Form and Server Actions
- Parse Server Action input: `schema.safeParse(input)` — handle failure explicitly
- Use `.trim()` on user strings; `.uuid()` for IDs

## Naming

- Components: PascalCase
- Functions/variables: camelCase
- Files: kebab-case
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE

## Imports

- Use `@/` alias for src imports
- Order: React/Next → external → `@/components` → `@/features` → `@/lib` → `@/types`
- Named exports preferred over default (except Next.js pages)

## Functions

- Explicit return types on exported functions and Server Actions
- Async Server Actions return `Promise<ActionResult<T>>`

## Forbidden

```typescript
// BAD
const data: any = await fetch(...);
// @ts-ignore
// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
```
